-- chem/vertex.cub — the volume operator at any vertex of a spin network, gauge-invariant or not, exactly, by
-- integer linear algebra. Each edge's representation of spin j is realised on the polynomials of degree at
-- most 2j in one variable z (Bargmann): J+ = −z²∂ + 2jz, J− = ∂, Jz = z∂ − j. On monomials every generator has
-- integer entries, so every J_I·J_K, every J_IJ², and every q_IJK = [J_IJ², J_JK²] (Brunnemann–Thiemann,
-- Class. Quantum Grav. 23 (2006) 1289, eq. 11) is an integer matrix; the basis is not orthonormal, but a
-- characteristic polynomial does not depend on the basis. The vertex's states are the invariants of the
-- tensor product: the weight-zero polynomials killed by the total J+. A vertex with an open spin-½ index
-- (where a holonomy has been attached, Thiemann QSD V eq. 3.8) is the same construction with one more
-- variable on which no q_IJK acts. So Q_v = Z Σ ε(I,J,K) q_IJK (eq. 9) is restricted to the invariants and its
-- characteristic polynomial computed exactly, over the rationals.
import "recoupling.cub"

